#
# Conformance case: teleology/fallback-combinator.
#
# A logic:Fallback is EXECUTED under executional entailment: the primary sub-program (primaryRoute) requires a precondition (primaryClear) that does NOT hold, so its executional entailment fails and the engine routes to the alternate (backupRoute), which runs and asserts rerouted. Nothing the failed primary would have done is emitted — there is no rollback because nothing was committed. Proves primary-fails-then-backup-succeeds, typed APART from action-level compensation.
#
# CRITICAL: the teleology evaluator seeds ONLY from input.nq world facts; this
# input.logic.ttl carries the minimal, clean-compiling, certifiable program axiom the
# projections need (no asserted teleology triples here — the world facts live in
# input.nq, exactly as the foundation conformance cases keep theirs).

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/teleology/fallback-combinator/> .

ex:GoalExpression a logic:GoalExpression .
